<title>GERMANY: Valeo workers in Germany protest to save jobs.</title>
<headline>Valeo workers in Germany protest to save jobs.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 570 workers at the Valeo SA plant in Heiligenhaus temporarily stopped work on Wednesday to protest against what they fear could be the closure of the plant, union IG Metall said.</p>
<p>The protest, which follows an agreement earlier this year to sharply cut the workforce, was driven by Valeo's refusal to guarantee that the plant will remain open, even after the job cuts.</p>
<p>Valeo bought the Heiligenhaus-based lock system division of Ymos AG around half a year ago and quickly sought to slash the workforce in half.</p>
<p>IG Metall said the protests would continue.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
